module uim.myname.application.adapters;
/// Application adapters for the application.
/// Application adapters act as intermediaries between the application layer and external systems or services.
/// They encapsulate the communication logic, allowing the application layer to interact with external systems in a consistent and decoupled manner.
/// By using application adapters, developers can isolate the application layer from changes in external systems, improving maintainability and flexibility.
/// In essence, application adapters provide a foundation for creating a flexible, maintainable, and high-quality application layer that can effectively support the evolving needs of the business.
/// Examples of application adapters include adapters for interacting with external APIs, databases, messaging systems, and third-party services.
/// Example: An adapter for interacting with an external API might handle the HTTP requests and responses, authentication, and error handling, providing a simplified interface for the application layer.
/// Example: An adapter for a database might manage the connection, queries, and transactions, allowing the application layer to perform data operations without dealing with the underlying database complexities.
/// Example: An adapter for a messaging system might handle message publishing and subscription, ensuring reliable communication between the application layer and the messaging infrastructure.
/// Example: An adapter for a third-party service might encapsulate the service's SDK or API, providing a consistent interface for the application layer to interact with the service.